    "updated_at": "2022-11-29T02:24:47Z",
    "body": "Editorially I've opted to use new serialization [[Type]] values of \"ResizableArrayBuffer\" and \"GrowableSharedArrayBuffer\". ~~The only difference is the addition of the [[ArrayBufferMaxByteLength]] internal slot.~~ After reading the section, since the internal slot list differ between resizable buffers and fixed-length buffers, having new tags seems easiest to read. LMK if a different style is preferred.\r\n\r\nEdit: I made a mistake in the initial PR. \"GrowableSharedArrayBuffer\" also has a separate data block for storing its length value (since it can grow in parallel). The newest commit fixes this, so multiple [[Type]] tags are probably warranted here.",
