    "updated_at": "2022-12-06T15:26:38Z",
    "body": "@annevk I would have thought any API that synchronously hits [get a copy of the bytes held by the buffer source](https://webidl.spec.whatwg.org/#dfn-get-buffer-source-copy) (like [Blob](https://w3c.github.io/FileAPI/#process-blob-parts)) would be okay for resizable input as it doesn’t keep a stateful reference to the original data block. Is there a reason this would be unsafe to permit or desirable to disallow?\r\n\r\n(If there is a reason it’s necessary/desirable to disallow it even when the data is immediately cloned, then [SubtleCrypto members](https://w3c.github.io/webcrypto/#dfn-SubtleCrypto) & and their pals would be prime test candidates.)",
    "author_association": "NONE",
